# profiles/secops.conf — Wazuh 4.5.4 on Elasticsearch 7 to Wazuh 4.14.7 on
#                        OpenSearch 2.19.5
#
# Copy to secops.conf and fill in. Never commit the real file.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ source
SRC_URL='https://10.9.9.4:9200'
SRC_NETRC="$HOME/.netrc.secops"
SRC_CA='/etc/logstash/certs/ca/ca.crt'

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ target
DST_URL='https://secops-new.internal:9200'
DST_NETRC="$HOME/.netrc.secops-new"
DST_CA='/etc/wazuh-indexer/certs/root-ca.pem'

DST_VERSION_EXPECTED='2.19.5'

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- notes
#
# Backfill engine: remote reindex is viable here (ES 7 source).
#   Prerequisite: reindex.remote.whitelist must include the source host:port
#   in /etc/wazuh-indexer/opensearch.yml on EVERY indexer node. It is a static
#   setting — rolling restart required. Schedule before backfill day.
#
# Cutover mechanism: Logstash output change.
#   The existing Logstash is load-bearing, not vestigial. It performs apiKey
#   redaction, data.trace type coercion, and fan-out to GCS cold storage.
#   Going native Filebeat would silently drop all three.
#
#   When rewriting that output: set manage_template => false. The 4.5.4-era
#   wazuh-template.json with template_overwrite => true would replace the
#   4.14.7 template the Wazuh install ships, discarding nine minor versions of
#   field definitions at the first connection.
#
# Known non-migratable: vulnerability history.
#   Wazuh 4.8 moved vulnerability state into wazuh-states-vulnerabilities-*.
#   On 4.5.4 that data lived in agent-local SQLite, so there is nothing on the
#   source to copy. It repopulates as agents rescan.
#
# Pre-backfill gate: mapping type conflicts.
#   Diff source and target wazuh-alerts mappings for fields present in both
#   with different types. Those documents get rejected or silently coerced.
#   See docs/RUNBOOK.md.
